<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Vocabulary in Context - How to answer</h1>
  <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
    <h2>How to answer</h2>
    <p>Read the whole sentence, not just the word.</p>
    <p>Look at the sentences before and after it for clues such as mood and tone.</p>
    <p>Choose the option that matches the meaning in <strong>this</strong> context, not the dictionary meaning on its own.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-green">
    <h2>Clues</h2>
    <p>Try to understand the situation or mood. That helps you eliminate options.</p>
    <p>The meaning may be hidden in the sentence.</p>
    <p>Notice the tone or emotion the word creates.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-pink">
    <h2>Key tips</h2>
    <p>Ignore words that only sound similar.</p>
    <p>Choose the meaning from this text, not from outside knowledge.</p>
    <p>Eliminate options that do not match the mood or the meaning of the sentence.</p>
  </section>
</div>
